## Usage rules

1. Every threshold must be labeled by model, effort law, closure, and operator.
2. Paper VIII's interval/collocation results refer to the 3S gated inner model only.
3. Paper VI's spatial modal cubic applies to local 3S frozen-A modes; its nonzero-mode results do not certify any threshold in this table.
4. Paper II's finite-donor primitive ledger has no interior positive-effort rest, so local Hopf thresholds from the working completion cannot be transferred to it.
5. Candidate-A instability at short delay is a zero-mode/DDE property; mean-field spatial equivalence does not make Candidate A stable for all delays.
